asel","mediatype":"movies","collection":["british_gov_public_films","ephemera"],"description":"A simple explanation of how peacetime taxes were spent paying for the enormous cost of the war.","date":"1948","year":"1948","subject":"peacetime taxes; world war two; great britain","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-07 09:35:53","addeddate":"2005-10-07 10:38:07","uploader":"florian@archive.org","updater":["nVIR","ewingrr"],"updatedate":["2005-10-07 09:56:21","2006-10-23 18:36:17"],"sponsor":"Central Office of Information for HM Treasury","publisher":"Crown Film Unit","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"9:41","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"9 Minutes 41 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"Straight forward explanation here about how your taxes work.. at the time, as the handy discaimer note at the end states. You see a little bit goes into \"War\", a little goes into \"Peace\" and a little goes into \"The National Debt\" Simple! If you're a bloke who just doesnt get it, then this is the film for you.","reviewtitle":"I see.","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-08-20 21:06:30","createdate":"2008-08-20 21:06:30","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"A nice piece of social education about what your taxes are used for.","reviewtitle":"Very Good","reviewer":"Dave Sands","reviewdate":"2016-01-23 16:16:34","createdate":"2016-01-23 16:16:34","stars":"4"}],"server":"dn800208.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn800208":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5416916801"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-04 17:44:33.161062"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":1101410080,"workable_servers":["dn800208.us.archive.org"]}